load @/code/structure/manifold
  find manifold

# A geodesic: the straightest possible path in a curved space, the shortest route between two points, the hyperbolic
# version of a straight line. In the Poincare disk geodesics are arcs of circles meeting the boundary at right angles;
# in the upper half-space they are vertical lines and semicircles centered on the boundary. Two geodesics that do not
# meet still drift apart exponentially, the signature of negative curvature. The form carries the manifold the geodesic
# runs in.
form geodesic
  link manifold, like manifold
